invariant: INV-14
file: srv_resume.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: a ticket issued after a resumed handshake carries the instant of that
  handshake rather than the instant the resumed ticket carried, so a
  client that keeps resuming holds a PSK for ever and the server never
  signs with its certificate again. srv_ticket.h carries the instant of
  the last full handshake forward for that reason. test/srv_resume_tests.h
  issues after a resumption ten seconds into the lifetime and requires
  the lifetime left to be ten seconds shorter.

--- old
    uint64_t auth_seconds = t->psk_selected ? h->ticket_auth_seconds : now;
--- new
    uint64_t auth_seconds = now;
